---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout page="index">
<main id="main-content">
  <section
    id="home"
    class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          Really Good Engineering Solutions
        </p>
        <h1>
          Practical technology consulting for messy, high-stakes
          environments.
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          RGE Solutions helps organizations turn unclear technology
          problems into working plans, cleaner operations, stronger
          controls, and better financial decisions.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a
            href="/contact"
            class="button primary">
            Start a Conversation
          </a>
          <a
            href="#services"
            class="button secondary">
            View Services
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel">
  <article class="signal-card large">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-engineering-clarity-822x500.webp"
      alt=""
      width="822"
      height="500"
      loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async" />
    <div class="signal-content">
      <span class="signal-label">
        Focus
      </span>
      <strong>
        Engineering clarity
      </strong>
      <p>
        Infrastructure, cybersecurity, cloud, data, vendors,
        and operating models brought into one practical plan.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-cloud-and-infrastructure-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      Cloud and infrastructure
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-cybersecurity-and-risk-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      Cybersecurity and risk
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-vendor-and-spend-control-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      Vendor and spend control
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="mini-card">
    <img
      src="/media/signal-ai-and-data-readiness-400x400.webp"
      alt=""
      width="400"
      height="400"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async" />
    <span>
      AI and data readiness
    </span>
  </div>
</div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="work"
    class="section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">
        What RGE does
      </p>
      <h2>
        Fix the gap between technology strategy and actual execution.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-stack">
      <p>
        Most organizations do not need more buzzwords. They need someone
        who can look across systems, teams, vendors, costs, risk, and
        delivery habits, then make the next right move clear.
      </p>
      <p>
        RGE Solutions works where engineering decisions affect business
        performance. That includes modernization, recovery work,
        integration planning, security improvement, platform cleanup,
        and executive-level technology advisory.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="services"
    class="section service-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Services
      </p>
      <h2>
        Built for operators, owners, and leaders who need traction.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="service-grid">
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          01
        </span>
        <h3>
          Technology Operating Model
        </h3>
        <p>
          Assess teams, platforms, vendors, processes, and decision
          rights. Build a practical model that supports scale without
          adding needless overhead.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          02
        </span>
        <h3>
          Infrastructure and Cloud Modernization
        </h3>
        <p>
          Stabilize core platforms, reduce technical debt, improve
          reliability, and map cloud, hybrid, or on-prem decisions to
          real business needs.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          03
        </span>
        <h3>
          Cybersecurity and Compliance Readiness
        </h3>
        <p>
          Clarify risk, strengthen controls, and prepare teams for
          standards such as NIST, CMMC, HIPAA, HITECH, PCI DSS, and
          related operating requirements.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          04
        </span>
        <h3>
          Vendor and Spend Rationalization
        </h3>
        <p>
          Find duplicated tools, weak contracts, unmanaged renewals, and
          unused capability. Turn spend into a controlled portfolio.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          05
        </span>
        <h3>
          AI, Data, and Automation Advisory
        </h3>
        <p>
          Separate useful AI and automation from noise. Identify where
          data, controls, workflows, and infrastructure need to improve
          first.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="service-card">
        <span aria-hidden="true">
          06
        </span>
        <h3>
          Program Recovery and Execution Support
        </h3>
        <p>
          Help stalled or at-risk initiatives regain direction through
          decision discipline, delivery routines, accountability, and
          executive visibility.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="approach"
    class="section approach-section">
    <div class="section-heading narrow">
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Approach
      </p>
      <h2>
        Simple enough to explain. Strong enough to operate.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Diagnose
        </h3>
        <p>
          Review the environment, listen to operators, verify the facts,
          and identify the decisions slowing progress.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Prioritize
        </h3>
        <p>
          Separate urgent noise from material risk, spend, reliability,
          and execution issues.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Design
        </h3>
        <p>
          Create a plan that leadership can fund, teams can execute, and
          operators can understand.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div
          class="timeline-dot"
          aria-hidden="true">
        </div>
        <h3>
          Drive
        </h3>
        <p>
          Build operating cadence, decision paths, vendor accountability,
          and outcome tracking.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section
    id="proof"
    class="section proof-section">
    <div class="proof-card intro-proof">
      <p class="section-kicker">
        Operating proof
      </p>
      <h2>
        Grounded in real recovery, modernization, and cost-control work.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-card metric">
      <strong>
        $25M+
      </strong>
      <p>
        Cost savings through governance, analytics, modernization, and
        financial controls.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-card metric">
      <strong>
        $115M
      </strong>
      <p>
        At-risk federal program stabilized through delivery recovery and
        operational discipline.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-card metric">
      <strong>
        100+
      </strong>
      <p>
        Sites supported across cloud, infrastructure, cybersecurity, and
        enterprise operations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
<section class="section founder-section">
  <div class="founder-card founder-card-with-photo">
    <div class="founder-copy">
      <div class="founder-label">
        Founder-led consulting
      </div>
      <h2>
        Led by Tim Gabaree
      </h2>
      <p>
        RGE Solutions is led by Tim Gabaree, a technology executive with
        CIO, infrastructure, cybersecurity, and operating leadership
        experience across government, healthcare, defense, private
        equity-backed, and mid-market environments.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work is intentionally practical: clear diagnosis, grounded
        recommendations, and execution support that respects both
        financial pressure and operational reality.
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://timgabaree.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-link">
        Learn more about Tim Gabaree
        <span class="visually-hidden">
          — opens in a new tab
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="founder-photo-wrap">
      <img
        class="founder-photo"
        src="/media/profile-pic-tim-gabaree-900x1200.webp"
        alt="Tim Gabaree, founder of RGE Solutions"
        width="900"
        height="1200"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
  <section
    id="contact"
    class="section contact-section">
    <div class="contact-box">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">
          Contact
        </p>
        <h2>
          Need a practical read on a technology problem?
        </h2>
        <p>
          Reach out for advisory, assessment, modernization,
          cybersecurity, vendor, AI, or execution support.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-actions">
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="button primary">
          Start a Conversation
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/rgesolutions"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button secondary">
          LinkedIn
          <span class="visually-hidden">
            — opens in a new tab
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Layout>
